/** @page dataframe_arrow_copy_behaviorguide Arrow, Parquet, And Copy Behavior

    @tableofcontents

    DataFrame Arrow IPC and Parquet APIs preserve logical schema and values
    across \c DataFrame, @ref Qore::SQL::ColumnarResult "ColumnarResult", and
    Apache Arrow. They use zero-copy storage only where ownership, alignment,
    nullability, and mutability rules make it safe. Mutating a DataFrame column
    that references external immutable storage detaches that column before
    writing.

    |!Data shape|!Import/export behavior
    |Fixed-width primitive columns|Preserved as dense buffers and can be zero-copy when host storage is compatible.
    |Boolean columns|Preserved as dense boolean buffers; Arrow bitmaps may be copied into Qore-compatible storage.
    |Fixed-scale decimal columns|Preserved as \c buffer<decimal128>; Arrow IPC and Parquet import/export can reuse the fixed-width buffer when precision and scale metadata match.
    |String and binary columns|Preserve values and schema; variable-width buffers may be copied into Qore-owned storage.
    |Date, timestamp, and duration columns|Preserve logical values and use \c buffer<int64> microsecond storage when represented as ColumnarResult/DataFrame dense columns; microsecond timestamp and duration Arrow arrays can be imported and exported without copying the value buffer.
    |List, fixed-size-list, struct, map, and dictionary-compatible columns|Preserve recursive schema metadata and lossless Qore values in \c auto columns.
    |Unsupported physical layouts|Raise an explicit I/O error or copy to a supported representation; they are not silently converted to lossy scalar strings.

    A DataFrame itself is intentionally not generic. Operations such as
    select(), groupBy(), join(), pivot(), and melt() can change the row shape
    at runtime based on selected columns or remote data. Use typed hashdecls
    for stable result records and \c hash<auto> for dynamic rows.
*/
